                                    <h2><span class="shaft"><img id="839-0" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_o.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Omnidirectional" title="Omnidirectional" ><img id="839-1" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_c.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Cardioid" title="Cardioid" ><img id="839-2" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_hc.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Hypercardioid" title="Hypercardioid" ><img id="839-3" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_8.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Bidirectional" title="Bidirectional" ><img id="839-4" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_wc.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Wide Cardioid" title="Wide Cardioid" ></span>Oktava MKL-012</h2>
                    
                    <h2 class="sub">                    Detachable-Capsule Pencil Tube Condenser Microphone</h2>
                    <p>The MKL-012 is a tube condenser head amp that accepts all MK-012 capsules. </p><p>The amplifier circuit is based on the Lomo 19A4 circuit. There is an output transformer within the external power supply.</p><p><img src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/mic_extras/oktava/mini_tube_box.jpg" class="thumb shaft" width="200" " alt="Oktava MKL-012 kit" />The tube is a subminiature triode, model 6&#1057;6&#1041;-&#1042;. (The Western designation is unknown at this time.) As in all subminiature tube mics, this tube is <em>not</em> socketed, but hardwired to the circuit board.</p><p>The MKL-012 is available in black or silver finishes. It ships with a dual-voltage (110/220) power supply, power cable, the microphone head amp, a metal mic clamp, and a -10dB detachable pad, in a padded wooden storage box.</p><p><img src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/mic_extras/oktava/mini-tube-psu.jpg" class="thumb shaft" width="200" alt="Oktava MKL-012 Power Supply" />Note: no capsules are included! Purchase any of the MK-012-compatible capsules separately.<p>The <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/Oktava/MKL-012">Oktava MKL-012</a> is also known as: Mini Tube.</p><p>The mic was released in 2008.</p>
